# Slab-based (SB) Ewald long-range dispersion for a planar LJ liquid-vapor slab.
# The smooth-damped slab kspace style pairs with the matched lj/cut/dispswitch
# pair style: the pair does the full LJ to r_cut and fades the 1/r^6 dispersion
# out smoothly over [r_cut, r_cut+Delta], while ewald/disp/slab adds the smooth
# r>r_cut dispersion tail with a 1-D (z) Fourier sum.  The real-space slab
# correction is folded into the reciprocal coefficients (no separate corr step).
# Fully periodic; no EW3DC kspace_modify slab.

units           lj
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p

read_data       data.lj_slab
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (10 10 36)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  1267 atoms
  reading velocities ...
  1267 velocities
  read_data CPU = 0.006 seconds

# matched pair: r_cut = 2.5, switch width Delta = 0.5
pair_style      lj/cut/dispswitch 2.5 0.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0

kspace_style    ewald/disp/slab 1.0e-4

# long-range surface tension gamma = (Lz/2)(P_zz - (P_xx+P_yy)/2)
variable        lz equal lz
variable        gamma equal 0.5*v_lz*(pzz-0.5*(pxx+pyy))
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal press pxx pyy pzz v_gamma
thermo          50

velocity        all create 0.85 4928 mom yes
fix             1 all nve
timestep        0.004
run             500
